### Artificial Intelligence and Machine Learning

You must not use the software or the content, in whole or in part, to train, fine-tune, distill, or otherwise improve any machine learning model, including any large language model, whether by you or through a third party, and whether or not for commercial purposes.

In particular, you must not:

- include the software or the content in any training, fine-tuning, or evaluation corpus for a machine learning model;
- use the software or the content to generate synthetic training data;
- use the software or the content for text and data mining, except for ordinary indexing of the public repository by a general-purpose search engine that does not train a model; or
- provide the software or the content to any person if you know or reasonably should know that the person will use it for a purpose that this section prohibits.

These restrictions do not apply to:

- using the software for its intended purpose, including use by automated coding agents that claim, check, or release files;
- a machine learning model processing the software or the content solely in its context window, without updating the model’s parameters, in order to help a permitted user install, configure, or use the software; or
- ordinary indexing of the public repository by a general-purpose search engine that does not train a model.

“Train”, “fine-tune”, and “improve” a machine learning model mean any process that updates the parameters, weights, adapters, or other learned state of the model using the software or the content, including pre-training, continued pre-training, instruction tuning, reinforcement learning from human or machine feedback, distillation, and similar processes. Processing text in a model’s context window without updating those parameters is not training.

The copyright license in these terms does not include any right to do anything this section prohibits. Any such right requires a separate written license from the licensor.

The licensor reserves all rights to make reproductions and extractions of the software and the content for text and data mining, including for the purpose of training machine learning models. This reservation is made in an appropriate manner, including by machine-readable means, for the purposes of Article 4 of Directive (EU) 2019/790 and any similar law.

Using the software or the content in breach of this section is a use of the software in violation of these terms.

